NEARS-1119 QA — blocking regression found in the fix

Repro: log into vendor panel as ahmed.khan@demo.com or demo.store@gmail.com,
GET /vendor-panel/business-settings/store-setup -> HTTP 500 for EVERY store,
not just the unit-less-delivery_time repro case.

laravel.log (worktree Admin/storage/logs/laravel.log):
[2026-07-16 10:45:43] production.ERROR: [FAIL] syntax error, unexpected end of file, expecting "elseif" or "else" or "endif" (View: /Users/Apple/Projects/nears-NEARS-1119-delivery-time/Admin/resources/views/vendor-views/business-settings/restaurant-index.blade.php) {"trace_id":"920da716d53385e0a2d08a3d3a6e4890","correlation_id":"6926ca1b-da4a-419b-958b-cec31c4d9b55","type":"Illuminate\\View\\ViewException","endpoint":"/vendor-panel/business-settings/store-setup"}

Root cause isolated via `app('blade.compiler')->compileString(...)` + `php -l` on the
compiled output: the file's PRE-EXISTING pharmacy-only inline directive at line 118
`@php($prescription_order_status = $prescription_order_status ? $prescription_order_status->value : 0)`
and every @if/@endif between lines 119-283 stop being recompiled into <?php ...?>
tags and are left as literal uncompiled text in the moment the fix's NEW block-style
`@php ... @endphp` (added at line 284) is present in the same file. Confirmed by
diffing compiled output with vs without the fix's @php block. Net effect: the
entire Store Setup page fails to compile for ANY vendor/store, not only the
unit-less delivery_time repro.

Independent verification this is NOT the pre-existing/unrelated PHP-8.5.6-only
issue claimed in the engineer envelope:
- Same result reproduced fresh on PHP 8.3.32 (Homebrew php@8.3, keg-only install),
  not just PHP 8.5.6.
- Swapped in the untouched base-branch (feat/human-review) version of this exact
  file, cleared view cache, hit the same endpoint as the same vendor/store ->
  got a DIFFERENT error: "Undefined array key 1" (View: same file) — i.e. the
  ORIGINAL bug this ticket targets, not the ParseError. The ParseError only
  appears once the fix's @php block is added back.
- Re-applied the fix (post-fix file restored, cache cleared) -> ParseError
  returns deterministically, both via HTTP and via `php -l` on the compiled
  view.

AC1 (store 2, unit-less "30-45"): FAIL — 500, ParseError (not the intended fix
behavior; also never reaches the unit-select-default logic).
AC2 (store 1, normal "30-40 min"): FAIL — same 500/ParseError; this is a NEW
regression on a path that worked before the fix on the base branch (confirmed:
base-branch file alone renders past this point for store-independent content).
